....................................13-23\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-2\n13\nPhone Settings\nHandset Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Phone settings\nChange User Interface Language\b\no Automatic 言語選択 → Select an item\nSet Time Zone Updating\b\no Manual only\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Time zone updating → Select an item → u (Save) \nChange Home Zone Time\b\no GMT+09: 00\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Home zone → g to highlight city → f (Select) \n→ u (Save)\n・\n Select the zone closest to your locality.\nActivate/Cancel Daylight Savings Time\b\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Home zone → g to highlight city → Highlight \nDaylight saving → u (Mark) → f (Select) → u (Save) \nSet Time\nDate & Time → Set date & time → In Time field, enter time → u (Save)\n・\n Some functions are disabled when time is not set.\nSet Date\nDate & Time → Set date & time → In Date field, enter date → u (Save)\n・\n Some functions are disabled until date is set.\nChange Time Format\b\no 24 H\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Time format → Select an item → u (Save) \nChange Date Format\b\no YYYY/MM/DD\nDate & Time → Set date & time → Date format → Select an item → u (Save) \nSet Time Correction\no Auto correction: On, Correction timing: Via S! Information Channel\nDate & Time → Time correction → Auto correction → On or Off\n・\n To specify when to correct the time, select Correction timing → Check an item → u (Save).\n・\n Selecting Manual correction → Yes immediately corrects the time.\nSet Earphone Settings\b\no Earphone\nEarphone settings → Earphone/Earphone + Speaker\nActivate/Cancel Prediction\b\no On Text input settings → Prediction → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Learning\b\no On Text input settings → Learning → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Auto Capitalization\b\no On Text input settings → Auto capitalization → On or Off\nActivate/Cancel Flexible Search\b\no On Text input settings → Flexible search → On or Off\nReset Learning Function\nText input settings → Reset learning → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-3\n13\nClear History for Pictograms/Emoticons\nText input settings → Clear history → Yes\nChange Font Size\b\no Standard Text input settings → Font size → Large/Standard/Small\nChange Cursor Speed\b\no Off\nText input settings → Auto cursor → Off/Slow/Normal/Fast/Very fast\nSave Entries to User Dictionary\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → New entry (If more than \none entry is saved, press u (Add) ) → Select Word field → Enter word or sentence → Select \nReading field → Enter reading → u (Save) \nEdit User Dictionary Entries\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → Select entry → Edit word \nand reading → u (Save) \nDelete User Dictionary Entries\nUser dictionary → Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → Highlight word → i \n→ Delete → Selected → Yes\n・\n To delete several words, select Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → i → Delete \n→ Multiple → Check words → u (Delete) → Yes.\n・\n To delete all the words, select Japanese dictionary/English dictionary → i → Delete \n→ All → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Yes.\nActivate/Cancel Simple Search \b\no Off\nSimple search → On or Off\n・\n On: In Standby, press keys assigned to characters used in Phone Book entry Readings.\nSet Any Key Answer\b\no Off\nAny key answer → On or Off\n・\n On: Press any keys except u, f, s, i, y and c to answer a call. \nAnswer Incoming Call by Opening Handset\b\no Off\nActive folder → On or Off\n・\n On: Open the handset to answer a call. \nSet Keypad Light Illumination Mode\b\no Normal mode\nKeypad light → Select item\n・\n Normal mode: Keypad light illuminates for Backlight time duration.\n・\n Saving mode: Keypad light turns off for set duration.\n・\n If Saving mode is set, in Starting time field, enter start time → In Ending time field, enter \nend time → u (Save).\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-4\n13\nSounds & Vibration & External Light Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Sound settings\nAdjust Volume\no Voice call/Message/Missed call notification/Delivery report/Phone \nsounds: Level 3; S! Quick News: Off\nVolume → Select item → s to adjust image\n・\n If Ringtone reducer is On (fP.13-10), Ringtone volume is reduced to Level 1 for the first four \nseconds, regardless of Ringtone volume set for Voice Call.\n・\n To mute Voice Call or Message tones, set Volume to 00 and Vibration to Off. \n appears.\nSet Ringtone for Voice Call\n\b\no Voice call: Samsung Tune\nRingtone → Voice call → Select save location for a file → Select a file\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback.\nSet Ringtone to Something Other than Voice Call\no Message: Good_morning; Missed call notification: Bubble; S! \nQuick News: Postman; Delivery report: Doorbell\nRingtone → Select item → Ringtone → Select save location for a file → Select a file\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback.\nSet Ringtone Duration to Something Other than Voice Call\n\b\no 5 Seconds\nRingtone → Select item → Duration → Enter duration → f (Select) \nSearch Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Music search → Follow onscreen instructions\nSet Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Settings → Follow onscreen instructions\nRegister/Cancel Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → Register/Cancel → Follow onscreen instructions\nView Instruction for Machi-Uta\n®\nMachi-Uta → What's Machi-Uta\nSet Vibration\b\no Off Vibration → Select item → Select a pattern\n・\n Press u (Play) to view a pattern.\nSet Phone Sounds\b\no Off\nPhone sounds → Keypad tones → Select item\nSet System Sounds\no Popup box alerts/Call end tone/Alerts on call: On; Minute minder/\nCall connect tone/Power on/Power off/Open/Close folder: Off\nPhone sounds → System sounds → Check items → u (Save)\n・\n Available items vary depending on mode.\nSet External Light Color for Incoming Transmissions\no Voice call/Missed call notification: Blue; Message: Green; S! Quick \nNews: White; Alarm: Pink; Delivery report: Light Blue\nExternal light → Incoming → Select an item → Select a color\n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-5\n13\nSet External Light Color for Notification\no Missed call/Missed call notification: Blue; Message: Green; \nAnswering Machine: Yellow; Missed alarm: Pink; Delivery report: Light blue\nExternal light → Notification → Select an item → Select a color \n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\nSet External Light Color When Handset is Closed\b\no Pink\nExternal light → Close folder → Select a color\n・\n When selecting Off, Notification light does not blink.\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\n・\n\tOpen Sound settings to change sounds for Normal mode. Settings cannot be changed for other modes.\nDisplay & Font Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Display settings\nChange Wallpaper\b\no Clover Wallpaper → (fP.2-5 Wallpaper b) \nSet/Cancel Smart Wallpaper\b\no On\nSmart wallpaper → On/Off → On or Off\nChange Wallpaper for Smart Wallpaper\nSmart wallpaper → Wallpapers → Select item → Select Wallpaper\nChange Main Menu Settings\b\no Standard\nMain menu style → Select an item → (g to select color, as required) → f (Select) \nSet Menu Color Theme\b\no White & Blue\nColor theme → Select an item\nChange Clock/Calendar\b\no Digital clock\nClock/Calendar → Select an item\n・\n If Digital clock is selected, in Style field, highlight style → In Position field, highlight position \n→ f (Save).\n・\n If Dual clock is selected, in First clock field, highlight time zone → In Second clock field, \nhighlight time zone → f (Save).\n・\n If Calendar (1 month) is selected, select Large/Small. \nSet Mini Clock\b\no Time only\nMini clock → Select an item\nSet Font Weight\b\no Regular\nFont → Font weight → Select an item\nSet Text Size in List Font\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → List font → Select item\nSet Text Size in Yahoo! Keitai Pages\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Yahoo! Keitai → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-6\n13\nSet Text Size in PC Site Browser\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → PC site browser → Select an item\nSet Text Size in Phone Book\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Phonebook → Select item\nSet Text Size in Editor\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Editor → Select item\nChange Message Text Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont → Font size → Messages → Select an item\nChange Text Scroll Speed for Menu List\b\no Normal Text scroll speed → Fast/Normal/Slow\nAdjust Display Brightness\b\no Auto adjustment\nBacklight → Brightness → i (Unmark) → g to adjust brightness → f (OK) \nSet Backlight Time\b\no 15 seconds\nBacklight → Duration → Backlight on → Select an item\n・\n When Backlight time is set to Off, Display becomes dim.\n・\n Display becomes dimmer when Backlight time elapses.\nSet Backlight Dimmer Time\b\no 15 seconds\nBacklight → Duration → Backlight dim → Select an item\n・\n When Backlight time elapses, Display turns off.\nSet Battery Saving Mode\b\no On\nBattery saving mode → On or Off\nSet Text Type in Dialling Display\b\no Normal\nDialling display → Font type → g to highlight type → f (Select) \nSet Text Size in Dialling Display\b\no Standard\nDialling display → Font size → g to highlight size → f (Select) \nSet Text Color in Dialling Display\b\no Basic\nDialling display → Font color → g to highlight color → f (Select)\n・\n If Monochrome is highlighted in Color field, select color.\nSet Background Color in Dialling Display\nDialling display → Background color → g to highlight color → f (Select) \nSet Operator Name\b\no Off\nOperator name → On or Off\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-7\n13\nManner Mode Settings\nSwitch Manner Mode\nf → Settings → Manner mode settings → Select mode\n・\n To edit each setting in Manner mode, highlight mode → u (Edit) → Set each item.\nCall Settings\nk\t\nf → Settings → Call settings\nForward All Calls to Voicemail (Handset Does Not Ring) \nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Voicemail on → Always (0 sec.) \nForward Unanswered Calls to Voicemail (Specify Ring Time) \nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Voicemail on → No reply (5 - 30 \nsec.) \nActivate & Set Forwarding\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Call forwarding on → Select an \nitem → Set number to forward (fP.3-14 Call Forwarding c) \nCancel Voicemail/Call Forwarding\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Deactivate All → Yes\nConfirm Current Voicemail/Call Forwarding Settings\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Get status\nListen to Voicemail Message\nOptional services → Voicemail/Call forwarding → Play voicemail → t or f \n(\n) \nActivate/Cancel Call Waiting\nOptional services → Call waiting → On or Off\nConfirm Current Call Waiting Settings\nOptional services → Call waiting → Get status\nActivate/Cancel Outgoing Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Outgoing call → Select an item → On or Off \n→ Enter Network Password → f (OK) \nActivate/Cancel Incoming Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Incoming call → Select an item → On or Off \n→ Enter Network Password → f (OK) \nCancel All Call Barring\nOptional services → Call barring → Cancel all barring → Enter Network Password → \nf (OK) → Yes\nConfirm Current Call Barring Settings\nOptional services → Call barring → Get status → Select an item\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-8\n13\nSet Missed Call Notification\nOptional services → Missed call notification → t or u (\n) → Follow the \nguidance \nCheck Call Time/Cost\nCall time & cost → All calls\n・\n To reset call time/cost, press u (Reset) → Enter PIN2 → f (OK).\nCheck Last Call Time/Cost\nCall time & cost → Last call\n・\n To reset last call time/cost, press u (Reset).\nCheck Data Counter\nCall time & cost → Data counter\n・\n To reset sent/received data counter, press u (Reset).\nShow/Hide Call Time/Cost after Calls\b\no Off\nCall time & cost → Show charge after call → On or Off\n・\n This function may not be available.\nChange Call Cost Currency\nCall time & cost → Set currency → Enter PIN2 → f (OK) → In Price field, enter rate in yen \n→ Select currency field → Enter currency unit → u (Save) \nActivate/Cancel Answering Machine\b\no Off\nAnswering machine → On/Off → On or Off\nSet Answering Machine Response Time\b\no 18seconds\nAnswering machine → Ringing duration → Select an item\n・\n If Other is selected, enter time.\nPlay Answering Machine Records\nAnswering machine → Play message → Select a record\n・\n To delete record, in list, highlight record → u (Delete) → Yes.\n・\n Alternatively, press t → All/Received → Select a record → u (\n) → Message.\nSet Answering Machine Response Language\b\no 日本語\nAnswering machine → Sound language → Select an item\n・\n Press u (Play) to play message.\nAccept/Reject Calls from Specified Phone Numbers\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Set reject number → On/Off → On or Off\n・\n When a call on Black list is received, the caller hears a busy tone and call is not connected. \nMissed call appears in Standby. Select the message to check missed call.\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-9\n13\nCreate/Edit Black List\nReject incoming calls → Set reject number → Black list → f (Add) (If more than one \nentry is added, press i → Add) → Select an item → Add an entry\n・\n \t\nTo delete a phone number, select Black list → Highlight party → i → Delete → \nSelected → Yes.\n・\n \t\nTo delete all phone numbers, select Black list → i → Delete → All → Yes → Enter \nPhone Password → f (OK).\nAccept/Reject Calls from Unknown Numbers\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Unknown → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls When Number is Withheld\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Withheld → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls from Payphones\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Payphone → On or Off\nAccept/Reject Calls When Number is Unavailable\b\no Off\nReject incoming calls → Unavailable → On or Off\nSave International Code\b\no 0046010\nInternational call → International code → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Enter an \ninternational code\nAdd/Change/Delete Country Number\no 日本 (Japan), 韓国 (KOR), イギリス (GBR), イタリア (ITA), \nスイス (CHE), スペイン (ESP), ドイツ (DEU), ポルトガル (PRT), \nオランダ (NLD), フランス (FRA), モナコ (MCO), アメリカ合衆国 \n(USA), スウェーデン (SWE), オーストラリア (AUS), 中国 (CHN), 香\n港 (HKG), 台湾 (TWN) \nInternational call → Country code → Add, change, or delete item\n・\n To add, press u (Add) → Select Country name field → Enter country name → In Country \ncode field, enter country code → u (Save).\n・\n To change, select country → Select Country name field → Enter country name → In Country \ncode field, enter country code → u (Save).\n・\n To delete, highlight item → i (Delete) → Yes.\nSelect Network to Access \b\no Automatic\nInternational call → Select operator → Select Auto/Manual → Select an item\n・\n When you set Manual, select a network.\nSelect Preferred Network from List\nInternational call → Select operator → Set priority → i → Insert → Network list \n→ Select a network\nAdd a New Preferred Network\nInternational call → Select operator → Set priority → i → Insert → New Network \n→ In Country code field, enter country code → In Network code field, enter Network code \n→ Select Network name field → Enter Network name → u (Save) \nSet Roaming Dial Assistant\b\no On\nInternational call → Roaming dial assistant → On or Off\n・\n If Roaming dial assistant is set to On, popup appears while dialing. If you add international \nnumber before phone number, popup does not appear.\nActivate/Cancel Offline Mode\b\no Off\nOffline → On or Off\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-10\n13\nShow/Hide Your Own Number\nCaller ID → On or Off\n・\n To check current status, select Get status.\nSet Handset to Automatically Redial Busy Numbers\b\no Off\nAuto redial → On or Off\n・\n On: Handset automatically disconnects call and redials busy numbers. Auto redial dials up to \nten times until i (Cancel) / y is pressed.\n・\n If called party uses Call Forwarding or Voicemail, call is forwarded accordingly.\nActivate/Cancel Automatic Ringer Reduction\b\no On\nRingtone reducer → On or Off\n・\n When Ringtone volume level is high, the volume level is reduced to Level 1 for the first four \nseconds, then returns to the set level.\nEnable/Disable Calling via Stereo Earphone Microphone\b\no Off\nEarphone call → On/Off → On → Call number → Select an item → Add a phone \nnumber\n・\n On: Press Stereo Earphone Microphone (optional) switch for 1 + seconds to call specified \nnumber. To change specified number, repeat setup operation, to save the new number.\nSet Clear Talk\b\no On Clear talk → On or Off\nAdjust Earpiece Volume\b\no Level 5\nHearing volume → s to adjust volume\nPhone Book Settings\nk\t\nf → Phone → Settings\nSelect Phone Book Save Location\b\no Phone\nSave to → Select an item\n・\n Always ask: Select save location each time a new entry is saved.\nChange Phone Book Preference (Phone/USIM) \b\no Phone\nChange view → Select an item\nChange Search Method\b\no ABC\nSearch method → Select an item\nSet Font Size\b\no Standard\nFont size → Select item\nCopy All Phone Book Entries & Save on Handset & USIM Card\nCopy all → Phone to USIM/USIM to Phone → Yes\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-11\n13\nMessaging Settings\nCustom Mail Address\nCustomize/Change Handset Mail Address\nu → Settings → Custom mail address → Follow onscreen instructions\n・\n Change mail account name (alphanumerics before @).\nDefault: Account name consists of random alphanumerics.\nS! Mail & SMS\nk\t\nu → Settings → Universal settings\nRequest/Cancel Delivery Report\b\no Off\nSending settings → Delivery report → On or Off\n・\n On: Receive a message confirming successful delivery of a sent message.\nQuote Text from Received Message\b\no On (Except SMS & Graphic mail) Sending settings → Reply with history → Select an item\nSelect Reply Setting\b\no Off\nSending settings → Reply settings → On or Off \n\t\nOn: Replies to sent messages are automatically addressed to \"Reply to\" address\n\t\nOff: Replies to sent messages are addressed to handset number/mail address\n・\n Set address that appears in To: field of message recipient handset.\nSet \"Reply to\" Address\nSending settings → \"Reply to\" address → Enter an item → Enter address\nChange Quick Reply Message\nSending settings → Quick reply setting → Select items → Enter message\nShow/Hide Transmission Progress Bar\b\no On\nSending settings → Sending progress → On or Off\nSet Received Message Notice Content/Hide Notice\b\no From\nReceiving settings → Message notice → View setting → Select an item\n・\n Received message notice scrolls above active function windows.\nSelect Secret Folder Message Notice Setting \b\no Show\nReceiving settings → Message notice → Secret folder → Enter Phone Password \n→ f (OK) → Select an item\n・\n Not show: Incoming message notice window for messages sorted to secret folders or \nMessage notice does not appear.\nLink External Light to Incoming Feeling Mail\b\no On\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Light color → On/Off → On or Off \n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-12\n13\nLink External Light Color to Incoming Feeling Mail\no Happy/Glad: Pink, OK/Good: Green, Sad/Sorry: Blue, NG/Bad: Light \nBlue, Important/Notice: Yellow\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Light color → Light color → Select a feeling \n→ Select a color\n・\n Press u (Check) to view color.\nLink Vibration to Incoming Feeling Mail\b\no On\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Vibration pattern → On/Off\nSet Whether to Sound Handset When Feeling Mail Arrives\b\no Off\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → On/Off → On or Off \nLink Ringtone to Incoming Feeling Mail\no Happy/Glad: Cheerful whistle , OK/Good: On_time, Sad/Sorry: \nRemember me, NG/Bad: Dear me, Important/Notice: Attention please\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → Assign tone → Select a feeling \n→ Select a save location → Select a Ringtone\n・\n Press u (Play) to playback the file.\nSet Feeling Mail Ringtone Duration \b\no 5 Seconds\nReceiving settings → Link to feeling → Ringtone → Duration → Enter duration \n→ f (OK) \nChange Font Size\b\no Standard\nDisplay settings → Font size → Select an item\nChange Scroll Unit\b\no Single line\nDisplay settings → Scroll unit → Select an item\nChange Received Message View\b\no Folder view\nDisplay settings → Received msg. view → Select an item\nChange Sent Message View\b\no Folder view\nDisplay settings → Sent msg. view → Select an item\nSet/Cancel Auto Delete for Received Messages When Received Memory is \nFull\b\no On (Except protected) \nAuto delete → Received msg. → Select an item\nOn (Except protected): Unprotected messages are automatically deleted oldest first to make \nroom for new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages \nand retry.\nOn (Only read): Read messages are automatically deleted from the oldest one to make room \nfor new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and \nretry.\nOff: Memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and retry.\nSet/Cancel Auto Delete for Sent Messages When Sent Memory is Full\n\b\no On (Except protected) \nAuto delete → Sent msg. → Select an item\nOn (Except protected): Unprotected messages are automatically deleted the oldest first \nto make room for new ones. If Auto delete is Off, memory full confirmation appears. Delete \nmessages and retry.\nOff: Memory full confirmation appears. Delete messages and retry.\nSort Unregistered Mobile Address as Spam \b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Unregistered → On\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-13\n13\nSort Message with Spam Filter\b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Unregistered → On\n・\n To specify list, Spam filter → u (Edit) → (If address already exists in the list, i → Add \nfilter) → Sender/Sender (Partial match)/Subject → (fP.4-14 Sorting Messages c) \nAdd Address to Permitted List\b\no Off\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Permitted list → On\n・\n To specify list, Permitted list → u (Edit) → (If address already exists in the list, i → Add \nfilter) → Sender/Sender (Partial match)/Subject → (fP.4-14 Sorting Messages c).\n・\n Available only when Unregistered/Spam filter is On.\nSet Address for Report Spam\t\n\b\no stop@meiwaku.softbankmobile.co.jp\nAnti-spam measures → Enter Phone Password → f (OK) → Address for report spam \n→ Enter mail address → Yes\nSelect Save Location for Message\b\no Memory card first\nSave to → Select an item \n・\n If Always ask is selected, confirmation appears each time a message item is saved.\nS! Mail\nk\t\nu → Settings → S! Mail settings\nSet Max Creation Size\b\no 2MB\nSending options → Max creation size → Select an item \n・\n In S! Mail creation window, press i → Sending options → Max creation size → Select \nitem can change maximum size temporarily.\nSet Message Sending Priority\b\no Normal\nSending options → Priority → Select an item\nSet Picture Auto Resize\b\no 500KB\nSending options → Picture auto resize → Select item\nSet Max Receiving Size\b\no 2MB\nReceiving options → Max receiving size → 2MB/300KB\nSet S! Mail Receiving Options\b\no On (Up to 1MB) \nReceiving options → Auto receiving → Select an item\n\t\nOn (Up to 1MB): Receives maximum 1 MB automatically.\n \nOn (Up to 300KB): Receives maximum 300 KB automatically.\n\t\nOff: Mail Service Center sends S! Mail Notice; retrieve complete message.\nSet Auto Receiving Condition\b\no All messages\nReceiving options → Auto receiving conditions → All messages/Specified address\n\n\nHandset Customization\n13-14\n13\nEdit Auto Receiving Condition\nReceiving options → Auto receiving conditions → Highlight Specified address → u \n(Edit) → Check item → f (OK)\n・\n If Individual address is checked, press u (Edit) → Select item → Select/Enter address/\nnumber/domain → u (OK).\nInsert/Hide Signature\b\no Off\nSignature → Auto insert → Select an item\n・\n To select Auto insert, Signature → Enter signature.\nEdit Signature\nSignature → Signature texts → En